    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d552">

                <pb facs="0497" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/98.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to
                            Haiti to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Haitian Minister for Foreign Affairs says that full powers were originally
                    given to the Haitian Minister at Washington; but if the Department does not
                    consider them to be such, and will outline the powers it desires him to have,
                    they will be issued at once, as the Haitian Government desires a speedy
                    settlement of the boundary dispute.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Furniss.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
